{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>For I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> Just as I am holy — for I am YHWH your Elohim — so 'you shall sanctify yourselves': sanctify yourselves below." "<b>And you shall be holy.</b> For I sanctify you above and in the World to Come." "<b>And you shall not defile yourselves, etc.</b> To transgress them in many negative commandments, and every negative commandment incurs lashes — and this is what they said in the Talmud (Makkot 16b): [If] he ate a putita he gets four [lashes], an ant — five, a wasp — six."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:00.482807159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}